    "body": "So I thought I'd do some of the wrapping for you, since it didn't all go according to the guidelines, but we also try to be a little more lenient with someone's first PR. However, it turns out you also wrapped things that this PR did not need to touch, such as\n\n``` diff\n+     <li><p>Let <var>notCanceled</var> be the result of <span\n+     data-x=\"concept-event-fire\">firing an event</span> named <code\n+     data-x=\"event-invalid\">invalid</code> at <var>field</var>, with the <code\n+     data-x=\"dom-Event-cancelable\">cancelable</code> attribute initialized to true.</p></li>\n```\n\n(This is wrong as you can wrap wherever there is a space. Wrapping directly after \"firing an\" as the text used to do is correct.)\n\nCould you undo that? Also, you can add your name to the acknowledgments.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
